From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add an OmniVision OV16880 sensor driver

The Mi MIX's rear camera is an OV16880 (OFilm module), which has no
mainline driver. Modes and register tables come from the phone's stock
camera library (libmmcamera_ov16880.so): stock init plus 2336x1752 (2x2
binned, 4 lanes at 768 Mbps) and the full 4672x3504 (1272 Mbps), with a
24 MHz XVCLK. The Rockchip ov16880 driver's register set produced no
frames on this module. Power sequence after the Rockchip driver,
structure after the mainline ov5675 driver.

Controls: exposure (lines, the low 4 bits of 0x3500-0x3502 being a
fraction), analogue gain, vertical/horizontal blanking, link frequency,
pixel rate, test pattern, flips.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig
@@ -453,6 +453,15 @@
 	  This is a Video4Linux2 sensor driver for the OmniVision
 	  OV13B10 camera.
 
+config VIDEO_OV16880
+	tristate "OmniVision OV16880 sensor support"
+	help
+	  This is a Video4Linux2 sensor driver for the OmniVision
+	  OV16880 camera.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
+	  module will be called ov16880.
+
 config VIDEO_OV2640
 	tristate "OmniVision OV2640 sensor support"
 	help
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/Makefile
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV08X40) += ov08x40.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV13858) += ov13858.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV13B10) += ov13b10.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV16880) += ov16880.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV2640) += ov2640.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV2659) += ov2659.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_VIDEO_OV2680) += ov2680.o
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov16880.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov16880.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov16880.c
@@ -0,0 +1,2332 @@
